gement with methotrexate: </strong></span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>- Success rate with local/systemic metho is 91%</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>- success rate decreases with beta HCG over 10000, positive fetal heart activity and gestational age &gt;12 weeks</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''><strong>Surgical management:</strong></span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>- More failure</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>,</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''> consider for women with life threatening bleeding, failed medical </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>management or unstable patient.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>- Dilatation and </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>curettage</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''> or hysteroscopic resection  with or without uterine artery </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>embolization</span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:159.8pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:106.