/strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> </span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Progressing towards </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>serosa – risk of rupture &amp; </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>hem</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>o</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>p</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>eritoneum</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:127.55pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong>TVS:</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong> </strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><u><strong>1st choice to diagnose</strong></u></span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><strong>- </strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>Empty uterine cavity &amp; Cervical canal</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>-  G.S / trophoblast mass @ scar