es of I/U pregnancy.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:127.55pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>1. Absence of Intra uterine G.S.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>2. Absence of </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>adnexa</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>l</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''> mass.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>3. G.S surrounded by bowel loops.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>4. wide mobility to fluctuation of sac </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>with</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''> TVS probe.</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>5. No fistula </span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''>6. No injury to tube/ovaries</span></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:11pt''><u><strong>MRI:</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-