<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[11218]" style="margin-bottom: 10pt"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Recommend antenatal high dose (50%, 75% or full therapeutic doses &amp; at least 6 weeks’ postnatal LMWH or until switched back to oral anticoagulant therapy.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>(Consider</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> x-a monitoring 0.5 – 1.)</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>These women require special management by experts in hemostasis and pregnancy.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Recommended antenatal and 6 weeks’ postnatal prophylactic LMWH.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Refer to local expert.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Consider antenatal LMWH.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Recommended postnatal prophylactic LMWH for 6 weeks.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Consider antenatal LMWH (but not routinely recommended)</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Recommended LMWH from 28 weeks of gestation and 6 weeks’ postnatal prophylactic LMWH.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Consider as risk factor and score approximately (see appendix III). </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Recommended 10 days if other risk factor postpartum (or 6 weeks’ if significant family history) postnatal prophylactic LMWH.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><em><strong>1.</strong></em></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> Previous VTE on long term oral anticoagulant therapy</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: #2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>- unprovoked</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: #2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>- E dependent.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: #2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>- idiopathic Very high risk</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><em><strong>2.</strong></em></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> Antithrombin deficiency.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>(Antithrombin</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> replacement @ initiation of labor.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>)</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><em><strong>3.</strong></em></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> anti-phospholipid syndrome with previous VTE.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><em><strong>4.</strong></em></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Previous </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>recurrent VTE.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Any previous VTE (except a single VTE related to major surgery).</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Asymptomatic high – risk thrombophilia homozygous factor V </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Leiden/ compound heterozygote.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Protein C or S deficiency.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Single previous VTE associated with major surgery without thrombophilia, family history or other risk factors.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Asymptomatic low – risk thrombophilia (prothrombin gene mutation or factor V Leiden) heterozygous.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Very high risk</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>High Risk</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Intermediate Risk</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Low Risk</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: #44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Table </strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: #44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>30</strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: #44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>. Guideline for thromboprophylaxis in women with previous VTE and/ Or Thrombophilia</strong></em></span></p>
