aphy</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:72pt;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>MCV &lt; 27 =&gt; High performance liquid chromatography</span></p><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 72pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+002D" data-source-marker-font="Calibri"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">-</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Female carrier =&gt; check partner status.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+002D" data-source-marker-font="Calibri"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">-</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Heel prick =&gt; neonate.</li></ul><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>3. Anemia, He</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>p</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> B, HIV, syphilis.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>4. Asymptomatic bacter</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>i</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>u</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>ri</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>a.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>5. Chlamydia – no test but information given</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> if age is </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>&lt; 25 years.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>6. Dating scan, 10 – 13+6 weeks (CRL </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>up to</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> 84mm, then HC).</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>7. Height, weight, BMI, B.P, proteinuria, risk factor for P</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>T</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>E, GDM.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>8. Screening for down to all women.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><em><strong>Combined:</strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> 11 – 13+6 weeks.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><em><strong>Tri</strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><em><strong>p</strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><em><strong>ple/ </strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><em><strong>Quadruple</strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''><em><strong>:</strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''> after 15 weeks.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>9. Identify genital mutation.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>10. Ask about past/ present mental health illness, depression.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>11. Occupation – identify occupational hazards.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>12. Support @ home – rule out domestic abuse, deprivation.</span></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:176.95pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family:"Calibri", sans-serif;font-size:12pt''>@ 16 weeks</span></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:362.55pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li dat