<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[22027]" style="margin-bottom: 8pt"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Reassess after 3 pulls</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Consider discontinuing the procedure:</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>If in vacuum – assisted birth the head is not on the pelvic floor (and birth anticipated with maximum 3 gentle pulls to ease over perineum)</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>If forceps birth and the head is not crowning with birth imminent with moderate traction, can’t applied easily, handles don’t approximate easily.</span></p>
